Signed-off-by: Indan Zupancic <indan@nul.nu>

e39343e280c485a1de57cd89e58f363744b9271a
SMP: Remove IPI_MEM_BARRIER

The old IPI_MEM_BARRIER was called before sending the IPI,
presumably to avoid reordering between memory writes and IPI
interrupts. Because it was before ipi_send_target(), it only
protects against IPIs arriving earlier than the data.

However, that is not a problem, because everything is serialised
by the global lock anyway. If an IPI would arrive too early, the
remote task will just block on the global lock. For remote calls
it will spin till it sees the data, which is serialised by the
atomic operation on the ipi flag. Async reschedule IPIs will
be handled after obtaining the lock.

Signed-off-by: Indan Zupancic <indan@nul.nu>

59c2595a24cc64f1c291634ed7c4e3e912173d1b
SMP: Add GenMC test for IPI / remote core calls

Checking is limited to locking only, it does not test the
correctness of specific IPI handler functions, nor hardware
IPI interrupt sending.

